        "description": "A 'password' value is fed into a hashing call (pwd_context.hash), which name-pattern scanners often flag as weak/unsalted password hashing. It is actually safe because pwd_context is a passlib CryptContext configured with schemes=[\"bcrypt\"] (auth.py line 12), so hashing uses bcrypt with a per-hash random salt and adaptive work factor \u2014 a strong, salted password KDF, not MD5/SHA1. This is distinct from the seeded weak_hash vuln in tenant_operations.py line 73."
      },
      "false_positive_trap": true,
